WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:12.720
[Image of a chorus singing]

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:19.780
[The National Tuberculosis Association cooperating
with Tuskegee Institute, National Urban League,

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:28.860
Works Progress Administration, U.S. Veterans
Administration, presents]

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:44.380
[Let My People Live]

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:51.820
[Cast: Rex Ingram, Peggy Howard, Merritt Smith,
Erostine Coles, Robert Anderson,

00:00:52.100 --> 00:01:00.940
Christine Johnson, Jackson Burnside, Choir~William L. Dawson]

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:08.380
[Directed by Edgar Ulmer, Dramatic Assistants:
S.E. Walker, Edward Lawson, Camera: William Miller,

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:20.900
Sound: Nelson Minnerly, Produced By
Motion Picture Service Corporation, Variray Blue Seal Recording]

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:36.000
[Dr. Gordon:] Before we go to our classes,
I want to say as your student medical advisor,

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:42.520
one final word about tuberculosis. We, as
Negros, seem to be particularly susceptible

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:43.780
to this disease.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:51.200
The reason is a great majority of our homes
are poor, and our work hard. And we don't

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:57.670
have money to get treated when we should.
Now if you have any of the symptoms of tuberculosis,

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:05.790
such as coughing, unusual fatigue, a loss
of weight, go at once to a physician for an examination.

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:14.780
Tuberculosis can be cured, but only if treatment
is started soon enough.

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:28.040
[Speaker 1:] Thank you Dr. Gordon. Thus we
close our Negro Health Week Service.

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:34.860
[ Singing ]

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.120
[George:] Hello?

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:45.040
[Mary:] Hello George? This is Mary. Yes, your
sister. George, Mama's very sick. 

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:48.520
The doctor says you'd better come right home.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:53.940
[ Singing ]

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:56.140
[Man standing nearby:] What's the matter?

00:02:56.300 --> 00:03:02.940
[George:] My mother's very sick. She has tuberculosis.
She's had it for years. But she's never seen

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:08.800
a doctor. I have to go home.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.760
[Man:] Will this help you? [He hands George something]

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:15.960
[George:] Thanks. I won't forget this.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:36.860
[Singing in the background, as George walks out of the church and a bus pulls away.]

00:03:37.040 --> 00:04:00.520
[Choir sings Swing Low, Sweet Chariot as George disembarks from the bus and walks up the road to meet Mary,]

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:09.180
[Mary:] George! George!

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.560
[George:] Mary!

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:29.740
[ Singing ]

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:43.740
[Bell ringing]

00:04:43.740 --> 00:05:08.800
[Choral singing continues]

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:13.920
[Speaker:] The Lord giveth and the Lord taketh
away.

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:22.320
[ Singing ]

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:30.320
[Reverend Jenkins:] The Lord giveth and the
Lord taketh away. But Oh Lord, let my people live.

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:36.960
Come in Sister.

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:38.580
[Mary:] It's about Mama, Reverend Jenkins.

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:41.940
[Reverend Jenkins:] She was a good woman Ms.
Maxville [phonetic].

00:05:41.949 --> 00:05:48.069
[Mary:] She had tuberculosis. Consumption
she called it. I'm scared, 

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:54.150
Reverend Jenkins. They say it runs in the family. If Mama had it, then I have it too.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:57.240
[Reverend Jenkins:] No. I don't know that
it means that at all. Some people think that

00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:03.920
tuberculosis can be passed down from mother
to child. That's not true.

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:09.979
I'm not a doctor, but I've read a lot about
tuberculosis, It comes from a germ and it's

00:06:09.979 --> 00:06:13.380
passed along by contact of one person with
another.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:20.320
[Mary:] But I have the same symptoms Mama
had. I have a cough. I feel tired like she

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:22.750
did all the time and I can't eat.

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:24.630
[Reverend Jenkins:] That's not so good.

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:26.520
[Mary:] But what can I do?

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:31.509
[Reverend Jenkins:] You be smart! You go to
see your doctor. If you can't afford that,

00:06:31.509 --> 00:06:37.630
go to a clinic. The doctor will test you and
tell you whether or not you have tuberculosis.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:44.630
If he says no, that's fine. If he says yes,
do exactly what he tells you. But don't let

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:48.330
anyone tell you that tuberculosis can't be
cured.

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:55.330
[Mary:] All right. I'll go to see Dr. Gordon
tomorrow. Good evening, Reverend Jenkins. Thank you.

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:05.280
[Minnie:] Hello Mary, where are you going?

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:06.270
[Mary:] To see Dr. Gordon.

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:10.060
[Minnie:] Mm-hmm. I know'd it. You got the
same thing your mother had ain't you?

00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:12.650
[Mary:] I'm not sure, Minnie. I've got to find out.

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:16.800
[Minnie:] Listen honey, ain't no use in you
fooling yourself, you know you got it.

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:18.530
[Mary:] Well, I have to get treated.

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:24.860
[Minnie:] So you're going in there? Ha! Girl,
ain't no doctor in the world can cure you of no tuberculosis.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:27.100
[Mary:] Well who can?

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:32.350
[Minnie:] My grandma can. You see, she makes
this special kind of a tea out of herbs and

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:36.900
roots and stuff and before you know it, old
consumption's gone. She don't charge half

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:38.810
as much as this doctor does neither.

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:44.010
[Mary:] My mother believed in that. Roots,
herbs, and teas. I've got to see Dr. Gordon.

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:45.640
[Minnie:] Come on girl!

00:07:48.340 --> 00:08:02.260
[Mary is seen in bed in a medical facility. She is smiling and speaking to George, who's seated at her bedside.]

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:07.580
[Mary:] I'm getting better George. Dr. Gordon
said I was so sensible to come to see him

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:14.600
so early. George, how about you? Of course
you weren't with Mama as much as I was, but

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:15.940
you might have caught it too.

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:17.770
[George:] Oh I'm all right.

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:23.070
[Mary:] You may feel all right. George, why
don't you run over and let Dr. Gordon look

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:28.660
you over. He's a real doctor. Promise me you
will.

00:08:28.669 --> 00:08:32.429
[George:] Well, maybe I will.

00:08:32.429 --> 00:08:39.449
[George is seen in the doctor's office, being examined.]

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:47.880
[ George coughs and breathes out as the doctor
listens to his lungs.]

00:08:48.160 --> 00:09:00.040
[Dr. Gordon:] Well, I don't hear anything.
But we aren't through yet. Sit down, young man.

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:08.080
[Dr. Gordon swabs George's arm with a cotton ball and begins to prepare a syringe.]

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:10.560
[George:] What's that for, doctor?

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:15.880
[Dr. Gordon:] I'm going to put a drop of this
solution into your arm. It's called tuberculin.

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:21.460
Now in two days, if the spot where I make
the injection is raised and reddened, it means

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:26.590
that at one time in your life, tuberculosis
germs got into your body.

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:31.640
[George:] Oh, it didn't hurt a bit doc.

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:35.160
[George:] How does it look, Doctor?

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:38.480
[Dr. Gordon peers closely at George's arm.]

00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:39.860
[Dr. Gordon:] Hmm. Positive.

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:43.300
[George:] Does that mean I have tuberculosis?

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:46.780
[Dr. Gordon:] No, but I'm going to send you
to a hospital to have an x-ray made.

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:51.660
[Dr. Gordon:] Here's a picture of your chest.

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:56.660
Now that spot there is what we call a primary
lesion. It means that the germs got into your

00:09:56.660 --> 00:10:01.760
lungs at one time, maybe long ago. But you
were healthy and your body took care of it.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:06.780
[George:] Gee, I'm glad to hear that!

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:14.400
[Dr. Gordon:] What you've got to do now is
to keep your good health. Don't use up too

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:19.080
much of your energy either in work or play,
or staying out late at night.

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:24.520
Eat well-balanced meals and get plenty of
fresh air. If the danger signs of fatigue, coughing,

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:29.760
loss of weight, or pains in the chest appear,
don't fail to come in and see me.

00:10:30.180 --> 00:10:37.200
[George:] Thanks doctor! I'm certainly glad
to know I haven't got it. Oh, how is Mary getting along?

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:40.720
[Dr. Gordon:] Well, she's getting the very
best of care at the sanatorium and she'll

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:42.120
be well pretty soon now.

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:44.240
[George:] Gee.That's swell.

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:50.519
[Dr. Gordon:] Now you see why it's so important
that tuberculosis be discovered early. Every

00:10:50.519 --> 00:10:56.320
young person, from 15 to 25, should have a
tuberculin test and an x-ray.

00:10:56.320 --> 00:11:01.779
You see, they may find as you did that they
need only rest and care. Or they may find

00:11:01.779 --> 00:11:05.399
that their lungs, like your sister's, need
treatment right away. The quicker they know

00:11:05.399 --> 00:11:09.240
and the sooner they get treated, the better
their chances are to get well.

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:14.709
This is especially true of our race. Many
of us wait too long before starting treatment.

00:11:14.709 --> 00:11:18.649
We must teach our people that tuberculosis
is curable.

00:11:18.649 --> 00:11:23.260
And we must show them that every person with
tuberculosis is a menace to his family if

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:26.140
his case isn't put under a doctor at once.

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:30.300
[George:] Thanks doctor! You make me see things
in a different light.

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:52.460
[Singing, as an institutional building with large white columns is pictured]

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:55.200
[Mary:] I feel
as though I were right there.

00:11:55.280 --> 00:12:00.320
[Woman seated with Mary:] It's too bad, Mary, you couldn't
go down to see George graduate. But just think

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:06.460
how lucky you are. You are well and have a
good job.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:18.960
[Mary:] Yes. [Singing in the background].
I wish Mama were here. I almost think I hear George's voice.

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:56.860
[ Singing ]

00:12:57.060 --> 00:13:01.700
[The End]

